		{
			description: [
				"The Apocrypha records the potion in three forms and only explains the first."
				""
				"Splashed, it reaches a person who did not agree to drink it."
				"On an arrowhead, it reaches one who is across a field and running."
				""
				"This is the entry the Convent argued about for a century. A mortal alchemist"
				"with a full quiver is the only thing in the world a rising god has to be careful of,"
				"and the god does not usually find that out until the second arrow."
				""
				"Nine civilisations produced someone who tried to become permanent."
				"Most of them were stopped by somebody standing very still, a long way off."
			]
